    <body>
      <pb n="1"/>
      <head type="main">tārāyaṇō</head><lb ed="bh"/>
      <head type="sub">kaï-bappabhaṭṭi-viraïya-gāhoccaya-rūvō gāhākōsō</head><lb ed="bh"/>

      <div type="section">
	<lg xml:lang="san-Latn"><lb ed="bh"/>
          <l><pb n="1A" ed="b"/><note n="1-1"><p><foreign xml:lang="eng">Begins:</foreign> ॥ 50 ॥ arhaṁ ॥</p></note>natvā sarvavidaṁ viracyata iyaṁ ṭīkēti tārāgaṇaḥ</l><lb ed="bh"/>
	  <l>kōśō ’yaṁ parayā pradōṣa-virahē ’pyābhāti kāntyā yathā</l><lb ed="bh"/>
	  <l>asmābhiḥ suvivikta-vākya-pavanairutsārayadbhirmahā-</l><lb ed="bh"/>
	  <l>mōhāmbhōda-tatīrjanasya manasi vyōmnīva nītē mr̥jām</l>
        </lg><lb ed="bh"/>
      </div>

      <div type="section">
        <head xml:lang="eng">Anthologist's homage to the poet's Muse</head><lb ed="bh"/>
        <lg n="1">
 	  <l>nandaü sacchanda-gaī nimmala-paya-pūra-gārava-mahagghō</l><lb ed="bh"/>
	  <l>jalahi-paḍiruddha-pasarō sukaīṇa sarassaī-pavahō</l>
        </lg><lb ed="bh"/>
        <p xml:lang="san-Latn">
          <s>sukavīnāṁ sarasvatīpravāhō nandatu</s>
          <s>sarasvatī vāk, tasyāḥ pravaha<lb ed="bh"/> ōghaḥ, sa nandatu</s>
          <s>kīdr̥g asau</s>
          <s>svacchandagatiḥ</s>
          <s>sukavitvādēva svādhīna<lb break="no" ed="bh"/>śabdārthatayā svacchandā aparāyattā gatiḥ pravr̥ttiryasya sa tathā</s>
          <s>saha<lb ed="bh"/> chandasā gāthādirūpēṇa vartatē iti sacchandā sā tādr̥ggatiḥ pravr̥ttiryasya<lb ed="bh"/> sa tathaiti</s>
          <s>punaḥ kīdr̥k</s>
          <s>nirmalapadapūragauravamahārvaḥ</s>
          <s>nirmalairapaśabdarahitaiḥ<lb ed="bh"/> padaiḥ suptiṅntaiḥ</s>
          <s>pūraḥ pūrṇatā tadgauravēṇa mahārghaḥ śrēṣṭhaḥ</s>
          <s>punaḥ jaḍadhī<lb break="no" ed="bh"/>pratiṣiddhaprasaraḥ</s>
          <s>jaḍadhībhiḥ pratiruddhō nivāritaḥ prasārō ’syēti</s><lb ed="bh"/>
          <s>sa hi yadi paraṁ jaḍadhiyō mūrkhān prāpya praskhalati, yadi vā prastāra<lb break="no" ed="bh"/>sthāpanāpēkṣayā jaladhinaiva pratiṣiddhaprasaraḥ</s>
          <s>ityēkō ’rthaḥ</s>
          <s>anyatra<lb ed="bh"/> sarasvatī nāma nadī tasyāḥ pravahastēna saha ślēṣō ’yaṁ vākpravahasya</s><lb ed="bh"/>
          <s>svacchandagatiḥ sō ’pītyarthaślēṣaḥ</s>
          <s>śēṣaḥ śabdaślēṣaḥ</s>
          <s>tathā hi</s>
          <s>nirmalasya<lb ed="bh"/> payasō jalasya pūragauravēṇa mahārghaḥ pūjyaḥ</s>
          <s>punaḥ jaladhinā pratiṣiddha<pb break="no" ed="bh" n="2"/>prasaraḥ</s>
          <s>nadyō hi samudramavāpya viramanti</s>
          <s>ētaduktaṁ bhavati</s>
          <s>sukavīnāṁ<lb ed="bh"/> vākpravahaḥ sarasvatīsaritpravaha iva nandatviti antarbhāvitaślēṣō ’<lb ed="bh"/> yamiti</s>
	</p><lb ed="bh"/>
	<note type="translation" xml:lang="eng">
        <p>
          <s>May the stream of the Divine Poetic Speech <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn" rend="parens">sarassaī</foreign> of good<lb ed="bh"/> poets flourish—the stream which operates according to its own will<lb ed="bh"/> and with choice metres <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn" rend="parens">chanda</foreign>, which is precious <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn" rend="parens">mahaggha</foreign><lb ed="bh"/> due to the dignity imparted by the wealth of flawless diction<lb ed="bh"/> <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn" rend="parens">paya</foreign>, and the flow whereof is blocked only by the blockheads<lb ed="bh"/> <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn" rend="parens">jalahi</foreign>; and which thereby resembles the stream of the river<lb ed="bh"/> Sarasvatī <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn" rend="parens">sarassaī</foreign>, which moves according to its own liking<lb ed="bh"/> <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn" rend="parens">chanda</foreign>, which commands reverence <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn" rend="parens">mahaggha</foreign> due to its mass<lb ed="bh"/> of overflowing limpid water <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn" rend="parens">paya</foreign>, and the onward flow whereof<lb ed="bh"/> is blocked only by the sea <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn" rend="parens">jalahi</foreign>. </s>
          <label rend="parens">1</label>
          </p><lb ed="bh"/>
	</note>
      </div>

      <div type="section">
	<head xml:lang="eng">Anthologist's homage to poets</head><lb ed="bh"/>
	<lg n="2">
	  <l>hiyayāĩ sajjaṇāṇaṁ rañjaï kasiṇēi khalayaṇa-muhāiṁ</l><lb ed="bh"/>
	  <l>savvaṁ suhāsiyaṁ pi hu jāṇa namō tāṇa sukaīṇaṁ</l>
	</lg><lb ed="bh"/>
	<p xml:lang="san-Latn">
          <s>sudhāsitam iti</s>
          <s>sudhā prāsādadhavalanadravyaṁ tadvat sitamapi<lb ed="bh"/> śuddhamapi yēṣāṁ kāvyaṁ sajjanahr̥dayāni rañjayati, khalamukhāni kr̥ṣṇayati,<lb ed="bh"/> tēbhyaḥ sukavibhyō namaḥ</s>
          <s>sitasya hi rañjanakr̥ṣṇīkaraṇē virudhyētē</s><lb ed="bh"/>
          <s>virōdhaścāyaṁ śabdatō nārthataḥ, <q type="pratīka" xml:lang="pra-Latn">suhāsiyaṁ</q> iti pada yataḥ subhāṣitaśabdā<lb break="no" ed="bh"/>dapi bhavati</s>
          <s>tēna yat subhāṣitaṁ kāvyaṁ tasya sajjanahr̥dayādirañjanā<lb break="no" ed="bh"/>dikamaviruddhamēvēti</s>
        </p><lb ed="bh"/>
	<note type="translation" xml:lang="eng">
          <p>
            <s>Salutations to the good poets: <seg rend="parens">it is a wonder that</seg> all of<lb ed="bh"/> their <seg rend="parens">creations</seg>, eventhough they are <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn">suhāsiya</foreign> <seg rend="parens">1. chunam—white,<lb ed="bh"/> 2, pure and excellent works of verbal art</seg> dye <seg rend="parens">2. give joy to, <foreign xml:lang="pra-Latn">rañjaï</foreign></seg><lb ed="bh"/> the hearts of the good, and blacken the faces of the wicked. </s>
            <label rend="parens">2</label>
          </p><pb n="3"/>
	</note>
      </div><!-- section !-->
    </body>    
